// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5548 update: windowsInstaller com object related rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5548
// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: PowerShell MSI Install via WindowsInstaller COM From Remote Location
// Sigma ID: 222720a7-047f-4054-baa5-bab9be757db0
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Meroujan Antonyan (vx3r)
// Date: 2025-06-05 | Modified: 2025-07-28
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1059.001, T1218, command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Detects the execution of PowerShell commands that attempt to install MSI packages via the
//   Windows Installer COM object (`WindowsInstaller.Installer`) hosted remotely. This could be an
//   indication of malicious software deployment or lateral movement attempts using Windows Installer
//   functionality. The usage of WindowsInstaller COM object rather than msiexec could be an attempt
//   to bypass the detection.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://informationsecuritybuzz.com/the-real-danger-behind-a-simple-windows-shortcut/
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/threat-intelligence/intelligence-insights-may-2025/
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f9710b0ba4de5fa0e7ec27da462d4d2fc6838eba83a19f23f6617a466bbad457
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/444a7d19c4e5be471aa81f4e62c2336034611932/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_comobject_msi_remote_install.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (((FolderPath endswith "\\powershell_ise.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe") or (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName in~ ("PowerShell_ISE.EXE", "PowerShell.EXE", "pwsh.dll"))) and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-ComObject" and ProcessCommandLine contains "InstallProduct(") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "http" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\\\")) and (not((ProcessCommandLine contains "://127.0.0.1" or ProcessCommandLine contains "://localhost")))
